Line 8: This is an amount in dollars, so it's never nothing.
        say row's tip plus $1, or $0.
            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
", or" gives another value when there isn't one. Leave it out here.

Line 9: This gives text when the cell is blank, but the column holds an amount in dollars.
        say row's tip, or "none".
                          ^^^^^^
The value after ", or" has to be the same kind as the one it stands in for.

Line 10: Only a column of numbers or amounts has blank cells that are nothing, but this is text.
        say row's day, or "someday".
            ^^^^^^^^^
